one of my favorite movies growing up was  the original mighty ducks now i don't  know if that's because i'm canadian and  it's required by law to like anything  hockey related or if i just like the  idea of being a kid and hopping into  strangers limousine but when i heard  disney plus was releasing a  10 episode series i was skeptical after  all the franchise spawned  three mega hit movies and even a one  season animated series  but when i started watching mighty ducks  game changers i was  pleasantly surprised this show is  actually pretty good so my inner  nostalgia got the best of me and i  decided to go back and re-watch the  original mighty ducks and see  just how different or similar these two  versions are  and let me tell you the show does a  great way of staying true to the  original while also  inventing new and fun ways to update the  franchise but before we begin make sure  to slap shot that like and subscribe  button  seriously only eight percent of you are  subscribed so that i can continue  watching movies of my childhood while  holding on to my last remaining  serotonin one of the biggest  game-changing events of the show and yes  the puns will get worse is that we don't  follow the mighty ducks at all in fact  this series takes place almost  30 years after the events of the  original and things  have changed for the worse in those 30  years the ducks have transformed from a  ragtag group of kids playing for the  love of the game  to a machine-like squadron built with  the sole purpose of winning  the kids on the team have personal  trainers follow strict diets and are  punished for losing  in essence the ducks in 2021 are like  how the hawks were  in 1992. it's a great role reversal that  sets up much of the conflict this season  the hawks even have an overbearing coach  named mr t  pity the fool no not that mr t he fills  the role of the must win at all costs  coach  both the movie and series are set in  minnesota following the 12 to 14 year  old district 5 hockey team's quest for  the championship  in the original coach bombay is forced  to coach a team as part of community  service for getting a dui  yeah that's something i totally missed  when i was 10 years old and what better  idea is there than getting a guy who got  a dui to coach your children  coach bombay does play a major role in  game changers but we'll get to him in a  bit  just like the original ducks were a  group of ragtag kids so too are the  don't bothers and yes that's the name of  the main team we follow named after a  line our main character's mother says in  a viral video of her chastising the  ducks for focusing only on winning for  her the ducks have sucked the fun out of  the game so she along with her son  evan who is kicked off the ducks decide  to start their own club in fact the  first episode is a lot like the first  act of the mighty ducks where they have  to go around recruiting members for the  team  the show could have gone the easy route  and recycled a lot of the tropes from  the original like recruiting the guy  who's good at slap shots or the figure  skater who can do some cool moves  but they don't opting to try new things  like the canadian student who ironically  doesn't know how to skate or the female  cosplayer who takes out her fury on the  ice  and even the characters who do resemble  their originals are given more fleshed  out backgrounds like kubler here the  goalie who resembles goldberg who has  parents who never see his games thus he  escapes reality by burying his head in  his phone all day when you have 10  episodes you can really learn and care  more about these characters so that when  the games do happen the stakes are much  higher  so alex morrow the mom from parenthood  and gilmore girls becomes the coach of  this new team but has to find a home  rink  enter the ice palace which was given to  coach bombay by hans and his will  you might remember hans from the  original as that old skate shop owner  and things have  definitely changed for coach bombay 30  years later and he absolutely hates  hockey  here's the long and short of it i hate  hockey and i don't like kids  he even has a sign that reads no hockey  how bombay went from beloved coach to  cantankerous old man is one of the  season's big mysteries  we'll later find out that his pro hockey  career which we see him leave for at the  end of mighty ducks  was cut short when he got an injury he  then went to coach collegiate hockey but  was fired after breaking the recruitment  rules by giving a poor kid money to  afford a stick  not quite sure how that works but c'est  la vie i  spent my entire life  chasing hockey and i have absolutely  nothing to show for it  so part of bombay's arc this season is  much like his original arc in mighty  ducks a dude who doesn't want a coach  learns to rekindle his love for the game  and become  loved by all in the process with it  being decades since the original game  changers  incorporates more tech almost all the  kids have cell phones and they're even  used as one of bombay's  unique practice exercises in the  original the kids use eggs to practice  their passing but in the show  it's their phones that's real ballsy for  a kid's movie mighty duck says no scenes  that take place at school but  game changers changes that all the kids  go to the same district 5 school where  their mascot is the frost  like the movie game changers keeps the  original district 5 teams  in hans's shop you can see a board in  the back that highlights them  this time we get full-on introductions  set with pyrotechnics and lighting and  i'm like this is sure hella different  than when i was playing hockey  it's here at the end of episode 1 that  the don't bothers announce themselves as  an official team  and just like the ducks the don't  bothers have literally no money and  their equipment is random stuff they've  been able to scrounge whereas the  original ducks get their equipment  donated to them by a generous grant from  mr ducksworth the lawyer boss of bombay  who the ducks are named after  the don't bothers break into the lost  and found at the ducks arena fun fact  alex  works at the same law firm that coach  bombay did with 10 episodes there's also  a lot more room to delve into the family  lives of our players with the exception  of charlie's mom in the 1992 version  there are almost no other parents seen  in the original in game changers not  only do we get a wide array of parents  but also different  family situations nick for example has  two gay parents  logan's parents are going through a  divorce and sophies are completely  overbearing i highly doubt that some of  the issues the show tackles would ever  have been addressed back in 92.  so with the team having their own rink  and equipment their first match is  against the cardinals in the original  the duck's first match is against the  hawks they end up losing 12-0  instead of 17-0 like the ducks did back  in 92.  the don't bother second game is against  the ducks and here they  actually lose 17-1 their only goal being  a new play that coach bombay  secretly wrote in alex's playbook in the  original coach bombay created the flying  v which they used to ultimately win  against the hawks this season introduces  us to  new and even more creative plays such as  the breakaway which involves shooting a  player into a group of others like a  bowling pin  and the double helix where players loop  around each other like a strand of dna  like the original game changer's main  kid has divorced parents with a dad who  is barely around  this allows for bombay to swoop in and  become this father-like figure for him  unlike the original bombay  doesn't end up kissing the mom however  there is some unresolved romantic  tension between the two which will  undoubtedly be explored in season 2. now  one of my favorite episodes this season  is where they bring back  actual members from the original trilogy  to inspire the new team  bombay's car window is smashed by fulton  just like it was in the original the old  ducks are back in town to attend the  duck's gala  gala bombay isn't invited to these  members include avermen  fulton connie guy and adam banks from  the original  and ken wu from d2 and d3 now you might  be asking yourself  where's charlie the main character from  all three mighty ducks films  played by joshua jackson well because of  coven and jackson having a baby it made  it impractical to have him appear  writer steven brill said that when they  do bring him back they want it to be  substantial  there's a lot of story to mind between  his relationship with bombay his absence  in the show is explained to bombay that  charlie didn't want to see a coach that  abandoned them initially brill wanted  all the old characters to have recurring  roles in the series like having avermen  be a teacher at the school  but kovit just made it too difficult  this is something that could be explored  in future seasons  speaking of averman he's now a limo  driver with a great callback to the  original as he drives the gang onto the  ice  the old ducks have a practice session  with the new ducks really linking the  two shows together  ironically enough the don't bothers get  their first win against the team that  was the strongest in the original the  hawks  this alongside their meeting with the  old ducks give them the boost they need  to continue their winning streak and  make it to the state finals bombay fakes  a power outage forcing the kids to play  classic pond hockey just like where he  met the original ducks and although the  kids have a love for the game  game changers adds romance between some  of the players  not seen in the original evan has a  crush on sophie and nick on geeky sports  announcer mary jo  unlike the mighty ducks game changers  builds up to the state championships  whereas the original was just for the  district this build-up is all for naught  when they don't bothers have to forfeit  because one of their players suffers an  injury and they need at least  10 players to play and with the ducks  winning out of a technicality the don't  bothers offer them a high-stakes game  on their own ice if they win they get to  take back the name  mighty ducks if they lose they have to  disband the team  forever and coach t is willing to play  dirty to win  not dirty it's hockey  just like coach riley was in the mighty  ducks i want you to drop banks like a  bad habit  i want it out of the game the don't  bothers end up playing with the original  ducks jerseys and win  using the famous flying v play to score  the game-winning goal the mighty duck's  name is officially in the hands of those  who stand for the spirit of the ducks  putting fun camaraderie and teamwork  ahead of winning at all costs now coach  bombay  doesn't get a kiss at the end of this  one but that's probably coming in season  2.  speaking of which there is no word yet  if the show has been renewed but with  the final shot being the ice palace  donning the mighty duck's name i sure  hope disney gives the second season  a shot yep that was another pun thanks  for watching everyone please make sure  to like and subscribe it really helps  the channel out and let me know what you  thought about mighty ducks game changers  for more bad takes you can follow me on  twitter and instagram at think story yt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

